<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila buys 1.63 mln bags of sugar to prop prices.</title>
<headline>Manila buys 1.63 mln bags of sugar to prop prices.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Food Authority said on Monday it had so far bought 1.63 million bags (50-kg each) of raw sugar at 610 pesos per bag to prop up domestic prices, Acting administrator Joemari Gerochi said in a statement.</p>
<p>The agency was buying raw sugar at 610 pesos per bag to bid up domestic prices which were at a low of 570 pesos before the procurement programme started in late February.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
